cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "gnss-audit: carrier-phase uncertainty audit and in-phase witness estimator for GNSS receivers under interference"
abstract: >-
  Code, experiment specifications and results of a study of whether C/N0-derived and receiver-reported GNSS
  carrier-phase uncertainties stay calibrated under radio-frequency interference. Truth comes from twin runs of GNSS-SDR
  on public jamming recordings, with and without injected interference, and from synthetic ghost satellites.
authors:
  - family-names: Woroszylski
    given-names: Julian
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ObvMamut/gnss-audit"
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-28
keywords:
  - GNSS
  - carrier phase
  - interference
  - jamming
  - uncertainty quantification
  - GNSS-SDR
